WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.959 --> 00:00:02.959
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie.

00:00:02.959 --> 00:00:04.540
Welcome back to my season 4 countdown.

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:06.420
Today we’re going to talk about some movies.

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:12.809
Recently George RR Martin revealed that Game
of Thrones movies are probably going to happen

00:00:12.809 --> 00:00:14.690
once the series is over.

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:18.062
Everyone involved kind of agrees that they
have at least 7, maybe 8 seasons worth of

00:00:18.062 --> 00:00:19.062
material for the tv show.

00:00:19.062 --> 00:00:21.939
So we’re talking 2019 before we’d ever
see one.

00:00:21.939 --> 00:00:25.679
The movies he talked about mostly had to do
with the expanded material.

00:00:25.679 --> 00:00:28.000
You know, prequel series he’s already done
work on like Dunk and Egg, the Blackfyre rebellion,

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.599
The Night King, you get the idea.

00:00:29.599 --> 00:00:34.079
All the awesome stuff you want to see but
they don’t have the money to do right now.

00:00:34.079 --> 00:00:38.312
With any luck, Game of Thrones will become
a much better version of what happened with

00:00:38.312 --> 00:00:39.649
the Star Wars universe.

00:00:39.649 --> 00:00:41.879
So here’s what we’re going to do.

00:00:41.879 --> 00:00:46.510
I’m going to count off my top 5 picks for
stories I think would make for the best movies.

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:47.879
Quick shout out for the countdown.

00:00:47.879 --> 00:00:51.480
If you’re finding me for the first time
I’m doing special countdown videos for the

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:52.480
season 4 premiere.

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:57.300
Be sure to subscribe to get everything and
leave me suggestions on videos you want to

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:58.300
see.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:00.800
My next one will be a Q&amp;A video.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:02.749
So leave your questions too!

00:01:02.749 --> 00:01:05.410
Here we go, Number 5 - The Hedge Knight.

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:07.130
Also known as Dunk and Egg.

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:11.920
Dunk is short for Ser Duncan the Tall and
Egg is the nickname for the future King Aegon

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:13.560
Targaryen the fifth.

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:17.450
The series takes place when Aegon was like
Bran’s age.

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:19.189
He was Ser Duncan’s squire.

00:01:19.189 --> 00:01:22.620
All of the Dunk and Egg stuff takes place
about 90 years before the current events on

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:23.700
the show.

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:28.909
Martin already wrote a novella in the Legends
Anthology for this.

00:01:28.909 --> 00:01:33.670
It became the first Dunk and Egg story that
was later turned into a comic book at Marvel.

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:36.930
So if you want to read a Game of Thrones comic
book you can do that right now.

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:39.080
It’s an ongoing series.

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:42.939
There are two other novella called Sworn sword
and The Mystery Knight.

00:01:42.939 --> 00:01:48.119
A fourth one called The She Wolves of Winterfell
is currently planned for another anthology

00:01:48.119 --> 00:01:49.370
this year.

00:01:49.370 --> 00:01:52.950
So Martin has already spent a ton of time
developing these characters.

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:57.229
This makes the most sense for a prequel movie
or even tv series.

00:01:57.229 --> 00:02:00.640
Plus they can re-use most of the costumes
from the show, just because it happens so

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:02.509
close to current events.

00:02:02.509 --> 00:02:07.430
The Dunk and Egg stories also overlap with
The Blackfyre rebellion, the Bloodraven and

00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:09.229
the War of the Ninepenny Kings.

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:14.000
So this material could really be the backbone
of a whole new series of movies, not just

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.000
one.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:18.950
As a side note, If you’re bummed that Winds
of Winter is taking so long to get here.

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:20.970
Just read all these anthology stories.

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:22.190
They’re awesome.

00:02:22.190 --> 00:02:24.450
Number 4 - The Blackfyre Rebellion.

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:29.050
King Aegon the Fourth, who was the worst king
in the history of Westeros.

00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:32.360
Legitimizes all his bastards, and one of them
makes a claim on the Iron Throne.

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:36.010
This becomes the second major civil war after
the Dance of The Dragons.

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:40.590
The primary characters are Daemon Blackfyre,
who started the rebellion, the Bloodraven,

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:43.560
his half-brother and King Daeron the second.

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:44.800
Interesting side note.

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:48.640
One of the other Blackfyre bastards escaped
at the end of all this to the east and formed

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:54.530
the Gold Company, one of the most famous groups
of mercenaries.

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:58.620
The whole thing started because Aegon the
fourth thought his son Daeron was secretly

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:00.420
fathered by his brother.

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:05.680
So he gave his valyrian sword called Blackfyre
to his bastard son Daemon.

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:06.680
Legitimizing him.

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:10.870
People kind of associated this really famous
sword that had been passed down from Aegon

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:14.010
the first, as a visual sign of the succession.

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:18.370
So when you gave the sword to someone, it
was like saying you want them to be king next.

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:20.590
And civil war blew up everywhere.

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:24.310
Remember though, there are a ton of huge characters
involved.

00:03:24.310 --> 00:03:25.720
Number 3 - The Bloodraven.

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:27.570
Ser Brynden Rivers.

00:03:27.570 --> 00:03:29.940
One of the other legitimized bastards of Aegon
the fourth.

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:32.500
There is so much story that his character
is involved in.

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:35.240
The first and second Blackfyre rebellions.

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:39.800
He was hand of the king for a long time, he
was present during all the Dunk and Egg stories

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:41.440
and he was a magic user.

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:45.530
He primarily practiced Glamouring, which is
changing your features.

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:52.680
But he also became the last greenseer and
may or may not be part of season 4.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:54.760
Of all the characters in a song of ice and
fire.

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:56.640
He is definitely one of the most interesting.

00:03:56.640 --> 00:04:00.040
I don’t want to include too many spoilers,
because a lot of his story spills over into

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:02.460
what’s happening right now.

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:05.590
But feel free to ask me about it in the comments.

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:07.350
Number 2 - The Dance of The Dragons.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:10.170
The first major Targaryen Civil War.

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:14.270
Martin actually just published this as a novella
in the Dangerous Women anthology.

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:15.750
That’s the short version.

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:19.250
There’s a complete history of the event
he’s writing for a new book after he’s

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:21.739
done with all the Song of Ice and Fire books.

00:04:21.739 --> 00:04:25.980
It’s called Fire and Blood and it’s the
complete history of the Targaryen house.

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:31.510
For this movie idea I’m mostly focusing
on the Dance of the Dragons event, but you

00:04:31.510 --> 00:04:32.510
get the idea.

00:04:32.510 --> 00:04:36.990
You could do a whole new tv series told exclusively
from the Targaryen’s perspective across

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:38.789
the entire history of Westeros.

00:04:38.789 --> 00:04:43.689
It’s not that there’s no good ideas, there’s
way too many good ideas.

00:04:43.689 --> 00:04:47.849
If you haven’t read the short story, the
Dance is just a civil war that started right

00:04:47.849 --> 00:04:52.889
after the death of the king and involved his
son and his daughter from another woman.

00:04:52.889 --> 00:04:55.400
And a whole lot of dragons.

00:04:55.400 --> 00:05:00.550
The real attraction of this story is that
it becomes a war fought on the backs of dragons.

00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:02.669
Mostly distinguished by their color.

00:05:02.669 --> 00:05:07.680
One of the big problems of the Targaryen succession
was that they engaged in the kind of sisterwiving

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:09.830
that Jaime and Cersei have been doing.

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:13.400
So when they cheated on each other, they did
it with other Targaryens.

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:18.910
So sometimes you had bastard children born
inside the royal line of succession, making

00:05:18.910 --> 00:05:21.139
things super complicated.

00:05:21.139 --> 00:05:26.840
and my Number 1 pick Filling in the gaps of
the current story.

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:29.800
Even though the show does an amazing job of
telling the book story.

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:32.240
It still has to leave a lot of things out.

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:36.009
An extra movie is an easy way to fill in those
gaps.

00:05:36.009 --> 00:05:40.460
Like telling the full story of Jon Snow’s
mother, Robert’s rebellion, and other things

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:42.940
happening that even George RR Martin hasn’t
paid off yet.

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:48.249
Martin will sometimes drop minor plots, like
the idea that Syrio Forel is really Jaquen

00:05:48.249 --> 00:05:50.160
H’Gar. Little things like that.

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:55.060
And most of the time on the show is dedicated
to things happening in Westeros, but you have

00:05:55.060 --> 00:05:59.120
the Frozen North beyond the wall and the East.

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:02.639
There are two more books coming and Martin
has said that we will get our first look at

00:06:02.639 --> 00:06:06.360
the distant North, called the Lands of Always
winter.

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:07.960
Guess which book that’s coming in.

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:12.789
But, using a movie right after the series
finishes season 8 would be a really easy way

00:06:12.789 --> 00:06:17.330
to mop up any loose plots that they didn’t
have the time or money to do during the seasons.

00:06:17.330 --> 00:06:19.090
Now it’s your turn though.

00:06:19.090 --> 00:06:22.430
If they start making Game of Thrones movies
which story would you want to see.

00:06:22.430 --> 00:06:26.919
Something with the current characters, or
a prequel story like Dunk and Egg?

00:06:26.919 --> 00:06:29.020
Remember, I’m posting my Q&amp;A video tomorrow.

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:30.720
Be sure to leave all your questions.

